CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*as102_dev)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct as102_dev_t)...)
#87: FILE: drivers/staging/media/as102/as102_usb_drv.c:363:
+	as102_dev = kzalloc(sizeof(struct as102_dev_t), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!as102_dev"
#88: FILE: drivers/staging/media/as102/as102_usb_drv.c:364:
+	if (as102_dev == NULL) {

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

